analytical_rust_port {
    Port ["../core-architecture.rq".analytical_package] to Rust: lexer, parser (index path), extractor, SQLite index, search, and export.
    `@reqlan/analytical` remains the published JS facade (`createAnalysisRuntime` / `AnalysisApi` / Zustand host state).
    Native work lives in a `crates/` Cargo workspace and ships as per-architecture binaries per [distribution.rust_binary_distribution].
    Langium LSP stays in ["../core-architecture.rq".language_package] / ["../core-architecture.rq".language_server] — this port is not a tower-lsp rewrite.
    Component plans: [rust_crate_layout], [lexer_rust], [parser_rust], [parser_align], [indexer.indexer_rust], [search_rust], [export_rust], [native_bridge], [cutover].
    @status in-progress
    @todo first `@reqlan/analytical-<platform>-<arch>` publish (Trusted Publisher on npmjs.com + analytical/v* tag)
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/tests/lexer.rs:prose_braces_stay_other"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/tests/parser.rs:keeps_inline_prose_braces"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/extract_parity.rs:indexes_scalar_list_block_and_flag_attribute_values"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/golden_corpus.rs:corpus_idea_names_match_langium_extract"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/langium-corpus-golden.test.ts:committed dump matches live Langium extract"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-search/tests/fuzzy.rs:ranks_exact_and_prefix_matches_ahead_of_subsequence_fuzzy_hits"]
    )
    @plan {
        goal
            Same AnalysisApi behaviour, faster and native, distributed as per-arch npm packages and per-target VSIXes without breaking the shared `<base>/.reqlan` index or the Langium editor.

        constraints
            - Ship per [distribution.rust_binary_distribution] and [distribution.vsix_export]: npm platform packages + host-targeted VSIX; website listing and GitHub-release postinstall out of scope.
            - On-disk ideas index schema stays compatible ([indexer.index]) so TS and Rust share application memory during cutover.
            - Grammar truth remains [syntax] / Langium; do not switch the language to tree-sitter (["../core-architecture.rq".grammar_and_parser]).
            - Port the context-sensitive lexer, not a naive parser-generator ([parser_lexer.lexer_bridge_to_syntax], [syntax_edges.nested_curly_braces], [syntax_edges.context_sensitive_lexer_scaling]).
            - Honour [indexer.nonblocking_index], [parser_lexer.parse_budget_timeout], [development_core.rust_mindset], [constitution.supply_chain].
            - Extension host loads the host-matching napi `.node` from the per-target VSIX ([distribution.extension_host_target]); missing core engine is a hard error (no sql.js fallback).
            - Interactive HTML graph/search JS and graph physics stay JS assets ([html_export.html_export_graph_layout]).
            - Comment-file indexing is [indexer.index_code_files] (native sync, not a Langium comment-grammar pass).

        steps
            1. Scaffold crates + CI + golden harness ([rust_crate_layout]).
            2. Lexer then parser with recovery and budget ([lexer_rust], [parser_rust]).
            3. Extractor + rusqlite index + incremental sync ([indexer.indexer_rust]).
            4. Search and analysers ([search_rust]).
            5. Export snapshot and writers ([export_rust]).
            6. napi-rs loader in `@reqlan/analytical`; CLI/MCP first ([native_bridge], [cutover]).
            7. Publish platform packages on `analytical/v*` and ship per-target VSIXes ([distribution.rust_binary_distribution], [distribution.vsix_export]).

        open
            - Language-server port remains Langium; CLI `parse` uses the core Rust engine.
    }
}

rust_crate_layout {
    Cargo workspace at repo-root `crates/` (not inside `packages/analytical`), crates:
    - `reqlan-parse` — lexer, parser, AST, recovery, parse budget
    - `reqlan-index` — extract, rusqlite store, mtime sync, diagnostics
    - `reqlan-search` — fuzzy / contextual / semantic ranking
    - `reqlan-export` — snapshot + html/md/json/csv writers; embed existing HTML JS assets
    - `reqlan-analytical` — facade matching `AnalysisApi` + `WorkspaceIndex` operations
    - `reqlan-napi` — Node binding for the core engine ([native_bridge])
    Mature crates only (rusqlite, napi): no experimental parser generators for the lexer.
    Golden tests compare Rust extract against Langium on the frozen [golden_corpus], plus the language-test fixtures ported into `reqlan-parse` / `reqlan-index` tests.
    Format: ["../development/commit.rq".rust_fmt].
    Root `pnpm test` runs `test:js` then `test:rust` from ["../../package.json"]. `test:rust` is `cargo test --workspace --exclude reqlan-napi`. GitHub CI compiles crates once, then runs `cargo test` as its own step so crate tests reuse that build (["../distribution/distribution.rq".ci_gate]).
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../package.json"]
        ["../../crates/Cargo.toml"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/golden_corpus.rs:corpus_idea_names_match_langium_extract"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/langium-corpus-golden.test.ts:committed dump matches live Langium extract"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/release-ci-gate.test.ts:pnpm test runs crate tests"]
    )
}

golden_corpus {
    Parser/extractor alignment uses a frozen `.rq` tree under `testdata/golden-corpus/`, not live product requirements in `reqlan rq/`.
    Production idea lists may change without regenerating the dump. Copy a representative file into the corpus and refresh `crates/reqlan-index/tests/golden/langium-corpus-names.json` only when grammar or extract behaviour needs a new sample.
    Langium and Rust both extract name+kind from that tree and must match the committed dump.
    Live parse alignment (elements and refs, both engines in one test): [parser_align].
    @status done
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/language/test/langium-corpus-golden.test.ts:committed dump matches live Langium extract"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/golden_corpus.rs:corpus_idea_names_match_langium_extract"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/langium-rust-parse-align.test.ts:golden corpus matches live Langium and Rust snapshots"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/parsing.test.ts:parse ontology.rq ideas"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/golden_corpus.rs:opaque_file_examples_do_not_extract_inline_or_fenced_paths"]
    )
}

lexer_rust {
    Hand-written Rust lexer that ports ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-token-builder.ts"]:
    structural vs prose `{` / `}`, fence opacity, quote-aware comments, `@` only at line start, glob `/**/` not a block comment.
    Linear in document size with sparse brace-depth lookup ([syntax_edges.context_sensitive_lexer_scaling]).
    Owned by `reqlan-parse`; consumed by [parser_rust]. Langium token builder remains the LSP lexer until a later language-server port.
    @status done
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/tests/lexer.rs:structural_braces_around_named_block"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/tests/lexer.rs:prose_braces_stay_other"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/tests/lexer.rs:glob_star_star_is_not_a_block_comment"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/tests/lexer.rs:at_only_at_line_start"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/tests/lexer.rs:url_slashes_are_not_line_comments"]
    )
}

parser_rust {
    Recursive-descent parser matching ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan.langium"] productions into a Rust AST the extractor can walk.
    Recovery: nameless `{...}` and local import mistakes still yield a usable document ([parser_lexer.recovery_vs_budget]).
    Wall-clock [parser_lexer.parse_budget_timeout] via native timeout/cancel — no Node worker process required on the index path.
    Dual-parser window: every grammar change updates Langium *and* `reqlan-parse` until the index path is Rust-only.
    CLI `parse` uses the core engine `parseReqlanSource` (`reqlan-parse`); Langium stays the editor LSP parser.
    Alignment contract: [parser_align].
    @status done
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/tests/parser.rs:keeps_inline_prose_braces"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/tests/parser.rs:recovers_nameless_block"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/tests/parser.rs:recovers_invalid_from_import_and_keeps_later_ideas"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/tests/parser.rs:times_out_hang_sentinel"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/tests/lexer.rs:mid_line_at_plan_brace_stays_prose"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/golden_corpus.rs:corpus_idea_names_match_langium_extract"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/golden_corpus.rs:tutorials_rq_keeps_ideas_after_nested_slides_lists"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/parsing.test.ts:keeps later ideas after nested @slides lists with mid-line @plan braces"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/parsing.test.ts:parse tutorials.rq nested @slides lists without parser errors"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/langium-rust-parse-align.test.ts:golden corpus matches live Langium and Rust snapshots"]
        ["../../packages/cli/test/runtime-engine.test.ts:parse command uses native parseReqlanSource"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/load-native.test.ts:exposes parseReqlanSource on the engine when present"]
    )
}

parser_align {
    Langium and `reqlan-parse` stay two engines until the language server uses Rust.
    Grammar truth is [syntax] / ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan.langium"].
    The same source must yield the same parse snapshot: top-level elements, live bracket and wiki refs, inline-code count, and fence count.
    One Node test runs Langium and native `parseReqlanSource` (`parseAlignSnapshot`) together. A committed name dump is not the only check.
    Related: [golden_corpus], [parser_rust].
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/src/align.rs"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/langium-rust-parse-align.test.ts"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-napi/src/lib.rs"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/src/native/parse-source.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/language/test/langium-rust-parse-align.test.ts:golden corpus matches live Langium and Rust snapshots"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/langium-rust-parse-align.test.ts:inline_code_file_example"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/langium-rust-parse-align.test.ts:inline_code_file_only_line_range"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/langium-rust-parse-align.test.ts:fenced_file_example"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/tests/align.rs:inline_code_file_example_is_not_a_live_ref"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/tests/align.rs:inline_code_file_only_line_range_is_not_a_live_ref"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-parse/tests/align.rs:fence_body_is_one_code_snippet_not_inner_refs"]
    )
}

search_rust {
    Port [search_reqs.fuzzy_search] (separator-insensitive ranking), [search_reqs.contextual_search] (hop-distance rerank), and [search_reqs.semantic_search] into `reqlan-search`.
    Same `AnalysisApi.searchRequirements` / `--context` contract ([cli.commands]).
    Activity-bar idea search uses `WorkspaceIndexRuntime.fuzzy_search` / napi `NativeWorkspaceIndex.fuzzySearch` so ranking stays next to rusqlite and only capped hits cross into JS.
    Mixed list includes indexed `.rq` file-name hits (`kind` `file`) and pages with `offset` / `limit` (`truncated`).
    Client-side highlight helpers used by webviews may stay in the TS `./fuzzy-search` export until a shared WASM/JS copy is needed.
    @status done
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-search/tests/fuzzy.rs:ranks_exact_and_prefix_matches_ahead_of_subsequence_fuzzy_hits"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-search/tests/fuzzy.rs:matches_across_separator_substitutions"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-search/tests/fuzzy.rs:fuzzy_search_reads_sqlite_and_returns_ranked_hits"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-search/tests/fuzzy.rs:ranks_file_name_hits_with_ideas"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-search/tests/fuzzy.rs:pages_ranked_hits_with_offset_and_truncated"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-analytical/tests/fuzzy_search.rs:workspace_index_fuzzy_search_ranks_without_exporting_catalog"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-analytical/tests/fuzzy_search.rs:workspace_index_fuzzy_search_includes_file_name_hits"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-search/tests/contextual.rs:nearer_ideas_rank_above_farther_with_equal_text_scores"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-search/tests/contextual.rs:reranks_using_graph_edges_from_context_seeds"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-search/tests/semantic.rs:ranks_name_hits_ahead_of_summary_and_tag_hits"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-search/tests/semantic.rs:scores_reference_labels_and_query_tokens"]
    )
}

export_rust {
    Port [export_reqs.export_pipeline]: `buildExportSnapshot` then HTML / markdown / JSON / CSV writers in `reqlan-export`.
    Interactive HTML JS (graph canvas, list filters, search bars) stays static assets bundled into the export — not rewritten in Rust ([html_export.html_export], [html_export.html_export_graph_animation]).
    Hosts still call `NativeAnalysisApi.exportHtml` / `exportMarkdown` / `exportJson` / `exportCsv`; they do not grow format writers.
    PDF remains print-HTML ([export_reqs.pdf_export]); [html_export.html_export_print_order_by] stays a product follow-up, not a port blocker.
    @status done
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/json_export.rs:json_export_lists_persisted_ideas"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:html_export_writes_ts_page_template_set_and_embeds_assets"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:overview_status_and_tag_rollups_link_with_filters"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:url_base_and_header_link_produce_root_relative_hrefs"]
    )
}

native_bridge {
    The Rust engine is the analytical core (parse, index, search, export, typed queries, git-dates, overview coverage, barrel plan) — not an optional addon.
    `@reqlan/analytical` is a typed napi facade (specta `generated.ts`) plus thin Node helpers (`createBase`, path utils, `SqliteIndexStore` wrappers over typed napi).
    It does not depend on Langium, `@reqlan/language`, or Zustand.
    Webview-only helpers (search highlight, filter labels, file-treatment, context signals/model, graph physics) live in the extension package.
    Interactive HTML JS stays in `crates/reqlan-export/assets`.
    Native owns: parse-for-index, persist, query, search, export execution, IndexService / WorkspaceIndex sync,
    and the index lifecycle FSM + status snapshot via `NativeWorkspaceIndex` + `NativeSqlDb`. The FSM
    (`opening`/`syncing`/`ready`/`error`), counts, in-memory sync progress/cancel, last error, file-index
    issues (cap 500), and the document-update / workspace-change rings (cap 50) live in `WorkspaceIndexRuntime`;
    TS reads them through `statusSnapshot()`. Durable diagnostics persist in `index-diagnostics.sqlite`.
    Consumers: [cli.cli_package] and MCP import `@reqlan/analytical/core` so they never load Langium;
    the extension host uses the per-target VSIX ([distribution.vsix_export], [distribution.extension_host_target]).
    The host-matching `.node` is required at runtime; there is no sql.js fallback.
    @status in-progress
    @todo publish first `@reqlan/analytical-<platform>-<arch>` release (Trusted Publisher on npmjs.com + analytical/v* tag)
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/load-native.test.ts"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/native-packaging.test.ts"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/native-headless-entry.test.ts"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/open-analysis-api.test.ts"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/native-export-request.test.ts"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-analytical/tests/export.rs:html_export_honours_graph_page_url_base_and_header_link"]
    )
}

cutover {
    Native engine is required for CLI, MCP, and the extension IndexService path (no `REQLAN_ANALYTICAL_ENGINE=js` escape hatch).
    Order: golden parse/extract → headless CLI `analyse`/`search`/`export` → MCP → extension via platform VSIX (host-matching napi `.node` required).
    Shared [bases.base] `.reqlan` DB is schema v4 rusqlite; fixtures verify reopen compatibility.
    Langium remains for the editor LSP only; the index path uses Rust parse/extract.
    @status done
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/schema.rs:opens_at_schema_version_4"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/schema.rs:schema_v4_columns_round_trip_git_count_and_mtime"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/schema.rs:schema_v4_file_reopens_after_drop"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/schema.rs:opens_sqljs_written_schema_v4_fixture"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/schema-v4-roundtrip.test.ts"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/open-analysis-api.test.ts"]
        ["../../packages/cli/test/runtime-engine.test.ts"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/native-headless-entry.test.ts"]
    )
}

port_phases (
    rust_crate_layout,
    lexer_rust,
    parser_rust,
    parser_align,
    search_rust,
    export_rust,
    native_bridge,
    cutover
)

ts_interface {
    The TS interface over the Rust functionality stays fully typed via specta (`crates/reqlan-analytical` `export-ts` → `packages/analytical/src/native/generated.ts`).
    Specta copies Rust doc comments. `export-ts` rewrites those `rq:` paths from crate-src depth to `packages/analytical/src/native` depth.
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-analytical/src/bin/export_ts.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-analytical/src/lib.rs"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/analytical/src/native/generated.ts"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/generated-native-types.test.ts"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-analytical/tests/export_ts.rs:committed_generated_ts_matches_specta_export"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-analytical/tests/export_ts.rs:rewrite_generated_ts_comment_paths_adds_one_hop"]
    )
}
